### Expected Behavior

After dismissing a message box shown via `showMessageBoxSync`, I expect the focus to either go back to where it was (preferable), or to at least be able to focus back into the window.

### Actual Behavior

Focus is broken such that I can't focus in input fields until I focus on a different window/application and focus back in. Reminiscent of other issues with native JS dialogs.

Double-clicking in the input field shows the highlighting,

### Testcase Gist URL

https://gist.github.com/pushkin-/90e08a1956b2b7262918c614d8935b94

### Additional Information

Related issues, but not quite the same: https://github.com/electron/electron/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aopen%20showmessagebox%20focus

Worked in 11.5.0 and 12.0.0-beta.14 and broke in 12.0.0-beta.16 and 12.0.0.

~Will post a gist when I fix github auth issues, but here is the code I'm testing with:~
Gist: https://gist.github.com/pushkin-/90e08a1956b2b7262918c614d8935b94

main.js:
```
 const { app, BrowserWindow, dialog } = require("electron");

  let window;

  app.whenReady().then(() => {
      window = new BrowserWindow();

      window.loadFile("index.html");

      window.webContents.on("will-prevent-unload", (e) => {
          const choice = dialog.showMessageBoxSync(window, {
              type: "warning",
              title: "Leave Site?",
              message: "Changes you made may not be saved.",
              buttons: ["Leave", "Stay"],
              defaultId: 0,
              cancelId: 1,
              noLink: true,
          });

          const leave = choice === 0;
          if (leave) {
              e.preventDefault();
          }
      });
  });

  app.on("window-all-closed", () => {
      if (process.platform !== "darwin") app.quit();
  });
```

index.html:
```
<input type="text" />
<script src="renderer.js"></script>
```

renderer.js:
```
onbeforeunload = (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  return false;
};
```

